  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\nThe current construction achieves C\u22480.38087, which is slightly above the target 0.38085. Our approach involves adaptive refinement through coordinate-wise projection and polynomial features to escape local optima. We combine:\n- Initial stochastic projection using Poisson processes to generate diverse samples\n- Hierarchical optimization: learned features followed by gradient projection\n- Dimensionality reduction through orthogonalization\n- Adaptive restarts guided by sliding window statistics\nThe key bottleneck in the baseline is premature convergence in high-dimensional space. Our method specifically targets convex relaxation inconsistencies near boundary regions.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\nVariables:\n- h \u2208 \u211d\u207f with h[i] \u2208 [0,1] \u2200i, \u2211h = n/2\n- Projection operator P(h) = clip(clip(h,0,1) + \u03bb(\u03b4h - h),0,1) where \u03b4h is orthogonal adjustment\n- C5(h) = max_k (np.correlate(h,1-h,'full') * (2/n))\n\nObjective:\nMinimize C5(h) subject to constraints\n\nWe use three function classes:\n1. First-order: \u2207C5(h) \u2208 \u211d\u207f\n2. Projected: C5_P(h) = max_k (\u27e8\u2207_{k} C5(h), P(h)\u27e9)\n3. Smoothed: C5_S(h,\u03b1) = (c\u2096 - \u03bc)^\u03b1 log\u2061(exp((c\u2096 - \u03bc)/\u03b1)) + \u03bc\n\nAll evaluated over [0,1] manifold with linear transformation\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\nStep 1: Initialize with parent vector if available (n=250)\nStep 2: Scale by dx=2/n and ensure \u2211h=100\nStep 3: Define update functions:\n- Orthogonality projection: h_new = (I - cc\u1d40/||x||\u00b2)h for perturbation\n- Feature extraction: \u03c6(i) = [i, i\u00b2, i\u00b3, cos(4\u03c0i)] (length 4)\n- Gradient handler with fallback differentiation\nStep 4: Maintain population of 100 solutions\nStep 5: Perform adaptive phase cycling:\n- 0-20%: Poisson-driven initialization\n- 20-50%: Feature-space gradient descent\n- 50-70%: Dimensionality reduction via PCA\n- 70-90%: Stochastic restarts\n- 90-100%: Final coarse-grained optimization\n\nIteration protocol:\n1. Ensure \u2211feasible(h)=n/2 (using iterative adjustment)\n2. For each point, sample 3 update vectors\n3. Assign priority based on \u2207C5 and window history\n4. Project to [0,1] with convergence check\n5. Score C5(h) and enforce feasibility\n\n4. Search choices and variations:\nBase parameters:\n- Learning rate: 0.01\n- Projection coefficient: 0.8\n- Temperature schedule: 0.99^k\nStrategies:\n- Local: 80% (L-BFGS-B 65%, SLSQP 35%)\n- Global: 20% (simulated annealing)\nFallback: 10% (random resampling)\nEach strategy triggered by plateau detection\n\n5. Computebudget and robustness:\nPhase durations:\n1. Initialization: 220s\n2. Feature training: 330s\n3. Dimension reduction: 110s\n4. Optimization: 440s\nTimeout handling:\n- Graceful termination from within phases\n- Check constraints if solution becomes infeasible (patch with ramped perturbation)\n- Maintain minimum solution diversity (10% if adversarial convergence)\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n- Verify eventsolidary([0,1] and \u2211/2 conditions using dual projection\n- Check C5 finite and \u2265 current_best-1e-12 against baseline\n- Resampling protocol: 3 restarts if no improvement in 50 steps\n- Ensure numerical stability by gradient clipping (|gradient|\u22645)\n\nFor n-point vector initialization:\n- If no parent: dist=2/n, sample(0,1) then adjust to n/2\n- With parent: multiply by Poisson(\u03bb=3) then project\n\nThe all positioned programmatically in n=250 space, ensuring no explicit patterns. Statistical properties maintained via randomized selection coefficients.",
